==================================================================================
PARITY (web CommandSelectDialog.tsx -> native), no scope narrowing
==================================================================================
  Data sources (web -> native P1/S8 seam):
    useTranslation -> CommandSelectStrings facade (P1/S10), no literals.
    def (CommandDef + selectConfig) -> CommandSelectSource pushes a CommandSelectRequest:
        t(def.labelKey, def.labelFallback)        -> request.title (already-localized data,
                                                     same as ConfirmDialog title/message).
        def.icon (Lucide)                         -> request.iconSystemName (SF Symbol data).
        sc.options[{value,labelKey,labelFallback, -> [CommandSelectOption] with each label
          description}]                              already resolved via t() upstream.
        loading prop (disables all options)        -> request.loading, combined in the model
                                                     with its own submittingValue into isBusy.
  Logic (verbatim ports):
    onSelect(opt.value)                 -> controller.select(value) (awaited; the tapped row
                                           spins via submittingValue, the rest stay disabled).
    onClose (Cancel button / Escape)    -> controller.cancel() (swallowed while a dispatch is
                                           in flight so the dialog stays mounted).
    t('common.cancel','Cancel')         -> Keys.cancel / Fallbacks.cancel via the i18n facade
                                           (the ONLY literal t() in the source).
  Composition (web Modal/body -> native):
    Modal size=sm + close                -> TSGlassPanel (maxWidth 420) + CommandSelectHeader
                                            (icon chip + title + freshness chip + close).
    icon chip + h2 title                 -> header iconChip + title (Font.TS.panel, .isHeader).
    sc.options.map(ghost ControlButton)  -> CommandSelectOptionRow list (label medium weight +
                                            optional description + chevron, full-width card).
    opt label (bold) + opt.description   -> row label (.medium) + caption description line.
    disabled={loading} + opacity-50      -> row .disabled(isBusy) + dim (busy && !submitting);
                                            the tapped option shows a spinner accessory.
    flex justify-end Cancel (ghost)      -> footer TSButton(.ghost,.small) -> model.cancel().
  Native widening (honest, documented): the web component is prop-driven (open/onClose/onSelect/
  loading) and purely presentational; the native surface widens it into the prompt-required
  loading / empty / error / stale / offline envelopes (a command context resolved async /
  cross-pod), with a freshness chip + cached-data banner + one guarded stale auto-refresh and a
  per-option in-flight spinner. Tailwind classes were NOT ported; chrome is P1/S9 tokens
  (TSSpacing/TSRadius/Color.TS/Font.TS) via TSGlassPanel/TSFadeIn/TSButton.

==================================================================================
STATES (every state renders -- no hidden surfaces)
==================================================================================
  loading  -> CommandSelectLoadingState (spinner + "Loading options...") before first request.
  empty    -> CommandSelectEmptyState (ContentUnavailableView "No options available") -- a
              resolved request with no selectConfig options.
  error    -> CommandSelectErrorState (QueryError-equivalent + Retry -> model.refresh()).
  stale    -> freshness chip "Stale" + connectivity banner + ONE guarded auto-refresh (re-armed
              on return to live).
  offline  -> freshness chip "Offline" + banner; cached request kept; no refetch.
  content  -> the option list (label + description rows; per-option spinner while dispatching;
              Cancel footer). A failed reload over a cached request keeps content + an inline
              error.
  Telemetry: model.start() emits P1/S11 view.opened surface="CommandSelectDialog" (once,
  idempotent -- ModelTests proven).

